      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Metabolic syndrome, defined as a cluster of obesity, hypertension, dyslipidemia, and insulin resistance/glucose intolerance, has been identified as a major risk factor for coronary heart disease in women. Nurses should increase their awareness of metabolic syndrome to help identify and treat the current estimated 47 million US residents who have metabolic syndrome."},
